 "command": "scripts/gguf_engine_submodule_decomposition.py --arm {ar,mtp} --arm-d1 \"prefill,ar\" --engine hipengine=hipengine:<d1>:<k3> --engine current=llamacpp:<peer>:<peer> --engine laurent=llamacpp:<peer>:<peer>",
 "date": "2026-08-30",
 "findings": [
  "AR decode is faster than both peers at all eight widths (34.1 vs 38.3 ms/step at C1; 81.9 vs 105.3 at C8).",
  "AR admission is slower than the peers at C1-C7 and slower than laurent at C8: it scales 302.4 -> 2320.7 ms across C1-C8 (7.68x) while llama.cpp current scales 223.4 -> 847.0 (3.79x), because our admission does not overlap requests.",
  "Every AR row we lose is admission: the whole C8 gap is admission delta while decode is ahead by 23.4 ms/step.",
  "On the K3 MTP arm our C8 admission (2311.9 ms) exceeds the peer entire 24-token C8 wall (2026.7 ms current, 1899.6 ms laurent).",
  "Two separate MTP defects set our MTP flat at ~31 tok/s: MTP cycles do not pack across lanes (flat ~85-107 ms per lane-cycle, so a wave cycle costs 107 ms at C1 and 680 ms at C8), and the native GPU-accept path loses ~40% of accepted drafts at width >= 2 (per prompt 0.65-1.00 at C1 vs 0.30-0.69 at C4, with C4 identical to C8 for all ten prompts). See worklog entry 20260830T025717.533327Z-lhl-w7900-mtp-accept-width-invariance-break-f7c44a.md."
 ],
 "hardware": {
  "gpu": "AMD Radeon Pro W7900 (gfx1100/RDNA3)",
  "host_role": "default development host"
 },
 "inputs": {
  "hipengine_admission": "/tmp/he-d1-clean/he-d1-clean.json (verdict failed only because a one-token arm cannot engage K3; AR walls content-exact, 10/10 cells)",
  "hipengine_long": "/tmp/he-c1c8-k3/c1c8-k3-packet.json (status complete, 80/80 engaged, budget-conformed, exact)",
  "peers_ar": "/tmp/qwen38-w7900-{current,laurent}-c1c8-ar-prefill.json (arms: prefill n_predict=1, ar n_predict=24)",
  "peers_mtp": "/tmp/qwen38-w7900-{current,laurent}-c1c8-mtp.json (single arm, n_predict=24)"
 },
 "kind": "w7900_q4km_c1c8_submodule_decomposition",
 "limitations": [
  "peer MTP packets carry only the 24-token arm, so peer admission/decode cannot be split on arm=mtp; peer decode_step_ms 0 and decode_tok_s_aggregate null mean NOT COMPUTABLE, not free",
  "hipEngine admission here is the one-token arm wall per lane, which is prefill-bound (measured GPU busy 287.0 ms vs 295 ms wall at 45 rows)",
  "AR admission rows by width (302.4/584.5/877.2/1172.4/1457.2/1746.4/2033.3/2320.8 ms) are pre-grouped-prefill: grouped prefill shipped at 72a29e9ad and this packet predates it. The linear 292 ms-per-lane growth measured here was serialized prefill, and it is gone. Recomputed C1-C8 rows, with hipEngine now cheapest at C4/C5/C7, are in 2026-08-30-w7900-q4km-c1c8-admission-decomposition-post-grouping.json. The mtp arm of this file has NOT been recomputed and must not be quoted as current."
 ],
